10
00:01:00,896 --> 00:01:02,796
[SPEAKER_01]: It makes things unclear.

11
00:01:03,617 --> 00:01:12,801
[SPEAKER_00]: If your mind is clouded, indolent, lazy, no perspective is because you made it so directly.

12
00:01:14,122 --> 00:01:21,226
[SPEAKER_00]: Even more so than if you were, say, you know, have a tendency towards desire too much or tendency towards ill will.

13
00:01:21,266 --> 00:01:25,908
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's also a result of your actions, but it kind of gets its own momentum.

14
00:01:27,566 --> 00:01:42,331
[SPEAKER_00]: But with this, like, the momentum is always directly sustained, the momentum of your indolence, if you could even call it momentum, through you choosing to not go against it, to not really just, like, pull yourself out of it.

15
00:01:43,351 --> 00:01:46,952
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why it's always practically manifested through, yeah,

16
00:01:48,422 --> 00:02:13,715
[SPEAKER_00]: Choosing out of a preference to, say, not think about certain things because, oh, they're a bit uncomfortable, or I can't deal with that now, or I'll address that later, procrastinate, you could get up when you wake up, oh, that's just... that would be a bit uncomfortable, so I shall rather just indulge in this completely unnecessary, slimy, sticky, heavy comfort that I'm currently in.

17
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:28,015
